`py -3` on Windows if `python` is not found; replace `<file>` with the path); if you had run `git add` or `git commit`, run it again after the cure. Deleting the file and running cure 1 is not offered: after `git add` it removes a CRLF but brings a lone carriage return back from the index (measured). `sed -i 's/\r$//'` is not offered: it is GNU-only and leaves a lone carriage return. The cures were not run on real Windows. Why only those two files, measured on 2026-11-13 with gitleaks 8.30.1 by turning one file at a time into CRLF in a clean checkout: `sonar-project.properties` makes `gitleaks dir` report the key line (`test_hygiene_scan_public` fails); `exceptions.txt` makes the `grep -v -E -f exceptions.txt` step of `lint.yml` keep every line (that CI step would fail; the tests read the file with Python and still pass); `.gitleaks.toml`, `patterns.txt` (`git grep -f` found the same lines) and the `requirements-*.txt` and `.in` files made no difference (`pip` was not run on the lock files).
 
